---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · LABORATORIES & ACADEMIC CLUBS — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — two of the brief's fourteen bullets: Laboratories and
 * Academic Clubs. They belong on one page because the school pairs them itself:
 * its own inventory groups "Inquiry rooms · academic clubs" together, and the
 * clubs meet in the rooms. The two standalone routes were an implementation
 * experiment; their verified content is merged here and the routes are retired.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ AN ARITHMETIC ERROR FROM THE SPLIT PAGES IS CORRECTED HERE.
 * /academic-clubs/ read "four inquiry rooms that work alongside the twelve
 * laboratories", and a draft of the Curriculum page had "twelve laboratories —
 * nine subject rooms and four inquiry rooms". Nine plus four is thirteen, and
 * the inquiry rooms are not additional to the twelve — they are INSIDE it.
 * The school's own enumeration (data/academics.ts:770) is explicit:
 *
 *   "Twelve laboratories: Physics · Chemistry · Biology · Mathematics ·
 *    Language · Geography · Srijan · Model UN · Active Learning · Robotics ·
 *    two computer labs"
 *
 * Count it: eight subject rooms + four inquiry rooms = twelve. The separate
 * `index` block groups them 9 + 4 because it also lists a General Science lab
 * the enumeration omits; this page follows the enumeration, which is the school's
 * own count, and says so.
 *
 * ⚠ THE LABORATORIES ARE PHOTOGRAPHED EMPTY and every caption describes a room,
 * not a lesson. The one exception is sb-chem-lab.jpg, which genuinely shows
 * students at the bench, and is captioned as that.
 * ASSET REQUIREMENT: the Robotics Lab, and the four inquiry rooms in use.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — this page is the INVENTORY. What is done in the science
 * rooms belongs to STEM, Robotics & Enrichment; the library's collection belongs
 * to Reading, Language & Library. No result or programme is repeated here.
 *
 * Composition: split (ivory, photo RIGHT — what a specialised room means) →
 * collage (paper, LEFT — the twelve, enumerated) → path (sand — the four inquiry
 * rooms) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcCollage from '../../../components/academics/system/AcCollage.astro';
import AcPath from '../../../components/academics/system/AcPath.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/composite lab/DSC_1255 copy.jpg';
import pBench from '../../../assets/photos/sb-chem-lab.jpg';
import pBio from '../../../assets/bio lab/DSC_1274 copy.jpg';
import pComposite from '../../../assets/composite lab/DSC_1259 copy.jpg';
import pActivity from '../../../assets/activity learning lab/DSC_1218 copy.jpg';
import pMaths from '../../../assets/photos/sb-maths-lab.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Laboratories & Academic Clubs — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="The full inventory at Sunbeam School Ballia: twelve laboratories including Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Mathematics, Language, Robotics and two computer rooms — four of the twelve being inquiry rooms."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Laboratories & Academic Clubs"
    standfirst="Twelve rooms, listed plainly — and four of the twelve are not subject rooms at all."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Teaching & Learning', href: '/academics/teaching-learning/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="The composite laboratory at Sunbeam School Ballia, its benches and apparatus laid out along the room."
    position="50% 50%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcSplit
      ground="ivory"
      side="right"
      ratio="wide"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="Why the number means something"
      heading="A room for<br /><em>one subject</em>"
      body={[
        'Twelve is only a number until you know what kind of rooms they are. The distinction that matters is <strong>specialised against general</strong>: a chemistry laboratory with gas taps, a fume path and reagent shelves is a different object from a science room with a sink at the back, and only one of them lets a class run a practical the board expects.',
        'Physics, Chemistry and Biology each carry <strong>board practicals from Class IX to Class XII</strong>. The mathematics laboratory is the one most schools do without — its purpose is to make mathematics something handled rather than only argued on paper.',
      ]}
      photo={pBench}
      alt={`Students of ${school} working along the chemistry bench, test tubes held over the burners`}
      inset={pBio}
      insetAlt={`A subject laboratory at ${school}, benches and apparatus laid out along the room`}
    />

    <AcCollage
      ground="paper"
      side="left"
      kicker="The inventory, as the school counts it"
      heading="Twelve,<br /><em>and four of them are not labs</em>"
      body={[
        'The school enumerates its twelve rooms by name, and the enumeration contains a detail worth pausing on: <strong>four of the twelve are inquiry rooms rather than subject laboratories</strong>. They are counted inside the twelve, not added to it.',
        'That is a real allocation decision. A school with limited rooms that gives four of twelve to debate, making, maps and open-ended work has chosen to spend space on the subjects that do not sit an exam.',
      ]}
      ledger={[
        { k: 'Physics · Chemistry · Biology', v: 'Three subject laboratories, carrying board practicals for Classes IX–XII.' },
        { k: 'Mathematics', v: 'Mathematics as a practical subject — the room most schools do without.' },
        { k: 'Language', v: 'Spoken language, recorded and reviewed. Set out on Reading, Language &amp; Library.' },
        { k: 'Robotics', v: 'Drone · 3-D printer · telescope · embedded systems. Set out on STEM, Robotics &amp; Enrichment.' },
        { k: 'Two computer laboratories', v: 'Junior and senior, 40+ machines each.' },
        { k: 'Four inquiry rooms', v: 'Geography · Srijan · Model United Nations · Active Learning — <strong>inside the twelve, not additional to them</strong>.' },
      ]}
      lead={{ src: pComposite, alt: `The composite laboratory at ${school}, apparatus set out along the benches` }}
      support={[
        { src: pMaths, alt: `The mathematics laboratory at ${school}, its models and charts set out on the working surfaces` },
        { src: pActivity, alt: `The activity learning laboratory at ${school}, its worktables set out for group work` },
      ]}
    />

    <AcPath
      ground="sand"
      kicker="The four, and the clubs that meet in them"
      heading="Rooms for the work<br /><em>with no right answer</em>"
      body={[
        'The school groups its inquiry rooms and its academic clubs together, and this page keeps that pairing, because they are the same thing described twice: a club is what happens in the room. Each of the four is named for a way of working rather than for a subject on the timetable.',
      ]}
      beats={[
        { k: 'Srijan Lab', body: 'Making and design — where an idea has to end up as an object.' },
        { k: 'Model United Nations', body: 'Debate, position papers and committee. A student argues a country’s case, not their own.' },
        { k: 'Geography Lab', body: 'Maps, instruments and fieldwork — the subject taken outdoors and measured.' },
        { k: 'Active Learning Lab', body: 'The school’s own description: work with no single right answer.' },
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Four of twelve,<br /><em>spent on the open questions.</em>"
      body="The school enumerates its twelve rooms and names the four inquiry rooms among them. It does not publish club membership, meeting times or who runs each one — and it has published no photograph of the Robotics Lab or of the four inquiry rooms in use."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
